      "writtenOn": "2025-06-17T14:37:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we either only want to hard code this dstBlendMode when `skipColorXform \u003d true` (to detect the drawShadow special case, and not impact any regular drawVertices pipelines that a user might trigger), *or* we should allow all primitive color blend modes to optimize to `AddFixedBlendMode` (matching how the finalBlendMode is handled.  This would create more specific pipelines for drawVertices but it\u0027s likely that the user knows how they want to combine their vertex colors anyways.\n\nFor now I\u0027m leaning towards including `skipColorXform` so we don\u0027t impact precompilation that heavily and we can expand drawVertices to use more hard-coded blend functions as follow up if we want to.",
      "range": {
